{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9xR4Wn5zfYYk3T53jJq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `Hijack()` in `response_writer.go` so it only refuses once body bytes have been written. Before, it also refused after just the headers were sent. The full test suite passes.\n\n**The problem:** `Hijack()` used to check `w.Written()`, which is true as soon as the headers go out, even with no body. Some websocket libraries, like `github.com/coder/websocket`, send the `101 Switching Protocols` status and then take over the connection. Under gin that failed with `errHijackAlreadyWritten`. Go's standard `net/http` allows hijacking after the headers are written.\n\n**The fix:** the check is now `w.size > 0`:\n- **Nothing written yet** (`size == -1`): hijack is allowed, and the writer is marked as written, as before.\n- **Only headers sent** (`size == 0`): hijack is now allowed. This is the new case.\n- **Body bytes written** (`size > 0`): still returns `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n\nThe old `if w.size < 0 { w.size = 0 }` line could never change anything, because the earlier check had already returned in every other case. It does its job again now. I also added a comment explaining the rule.\n\n**Test:** I added a case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite` called \"hijack after header write should succeed\". It sets status 101, sends the headers, then hijacks. The existing cases for \"before write\" and \"after body write\" still pass.\n\nNothing is committed yet, and the repo is on a detached HEAD. If you want, I'll create a branch and commit with `fix(response): refine hijack behavior for response lifecycle`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":34788,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":297,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebe1d093-a053-4eca-b574-1fa0b6248186","uuid":"2d86b4a2-1c74-4233-bac3-dd98a08d86f8","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:41:26.922Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9xR4JNx1DAeZ46rFh5G"}
